# Supabase — Clink
#
# Both values are safe to commit. A publishable key is designed to be
# embedded in a client app; Row Level Security (see supabase/schema.sql)
# is what actually protects the data. The secret / service_role key must
# NEVER appear in this file or anywhere in the app bundle.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ prefixed vars are inlined into the bundle at build time,
# so the Release build picks these up without any extra wiring.

EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://yklknprzyoebzgazcmhj.supabase.co
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_KEY=sb_publishable_nt7pkmBI-UA2u7S-ewFcYg_jprf697w

# Sign in with Apple and Continue with Facebook — which buttons this build
# shows. 'on' shows one; anything else hides it. Both stay off until the
# setup below is done, because a button whose provider is not configured
# fails on the first tap. Facebook only ever appears beside Apple (App
# Review guideline 4.8), so Facebook on with Apple off shows neither sign-in
# button; it does show Connect Facebook in Find friends for accounts that
# already exist.
#
# Apple needs a native build that carries the Sign in with Apple entitlement
# (app.json: ios.usesAppleSignIn and the expo-apple-authentication plugin).
# Once that build is out, flipping either flag is a JS-only change.
#
# Before 'on':
#   1. Supabase SQL editor: apply supabase/migrations/015_social_sign_in.sql.
#   2. Supabase > Authentication > Sign In / Providers > Apple: enabled, with
#      com.janmcqueeny.drinkdex among the Client IDs.
#   3. Meta for Developers: a Facebook Login app. Its App ID and App Secret go
#      into Supabase > Authentication > Sign In / Providers > Facebook, and the
#      callback URL that page shows goes into the Meta app's Valid OAuth
#      Redirect URIs.
#   4. Supabase > Authentication > URL Configuration > Redirect URLs: add
#      drinkdex://auth/callback.
#   5. Supabase > Authentication > Sign In / Providers: turn on "Allow manual
#      linking", which Connect Facebook (linkIdentity) needs.
#   6. Meta App Review for the user_friends permission, which needs the
#      privacy policy URL and a data deletion instructions URL. Until it
#      passes, only people with a role on the Meta app get a friends list.
EXPO_PUBLIC_APPLE_SIGN_IN=on
EXPO_PUBLIC_FACEBOOK_SIGN_IN=on

# Phone number (SMS code) and Continue with Google. 'on' shows one.
# Google, like Facebook, only ever appears beside Apple (guideline 4.8).
# Phone is first-party and shows on its own; with it off the top field is
# email. Both are JS-only flags: an EAS Update or the next build carries them.
# Before 'on' see specs/02-auth-login.md section 18 (Twilio Verify in Supabase
# > Phone; Google Cloud OAuth client in Supabase > Google), and apply
# supabase/migrations/016_sign_in_lookup.sql before any build ships.
EXPO_PUBLIC_PHONE_SIGN_IN=off
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_SIGN_IN=on

# Reels (short videos). 'on' shows the Reels tab, the Reels tab on profiles
# and the recorder; anything else hides all three. Needs a native build that
# contains expo-camera (the first build after 11); from that build on it is a
# JS-only flag. Before 'on':
#   1. Supabase SQL editor: apply supabase/migrations/019_reels.sql and run
#      its VERIFY block.
#   2. Record, post, watch, report and delete one reel on a real iPhone.
#   3. Upgrade Supabase to Pro the day a build with this on is public on the
#      App Store (specs/05-reels.md section 12.3). Until then the limits in
#      section 1 of 019 hold each account to 3 reels per 24 hours and 20
#      live reels; raise them there, with the copy's fallbacks
#      (REEL_DAY_LIMIT, REEL_LIVE_LIMIT in src/lib/reels.ts).
EXPO_PUBLIC_REELS=off

# Music on stories (Apple Music 30-second previews). 'tap' shows a song tag
# on a story whose preview plays only when the viewer taps it, with its
# "Listen on Apple Music" link (recommended: a preview of that song is what
# App Review 5.2.5 allows previews for). 'autoplay' plays the preview while
# the story is shown, with a mute control: do NOT ship it without written
# permission from Apple or the rights-holders (5.2.5 names background music
# under photos as the use previews may not serve; 4.5.2 needs sync rights).
# Anything else hides Add music on the Log sheet and every song tag. JS-only:
# an EAS Update can flip it, since previews play through expo-video, which is
# already in the binary.
#
# Before 'tap' or 'autoplay':
#   1. Supabase SQL editor: apply supabase/migrations/020_tournaments_and_story_music.sql
#      and run its VERIFY block.
#   2. Apple Developer: a Media ID with MusicKit, and a key with Media
#      Services (MusicKit) enabled for it; download the .p8 once, note the
#      Key ID and the Team ID. Never put the .p8 in the repo.
#   3. Supabase > Edge Functions: deploy supabase/functions/apple-music/index.ts
#      as 'apple-music' with Verify JWT on, and add the secrets
#      MUSICKIT_KEY_P8 (the whole .p8 text), MUSICKIT_KEY_ID and APPLE_TEAM_ID.
#   4. Add Apple's "Listen on Apple Music" badge (white and black) under
#      assets/images/ and swap it into components/songs.tsx (spec v3.1 §13.3).
#   5. Read App Review guideline 5.2.5, then post a song and play it on a
#      Release build.
EXPO_PUBLIC_STORY_MUSIC=off
